{"title":"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> denotes a polynomial of degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4c0efa59cf43ae9af6aa6db9c74ff752004728b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(k)=\\frac{k}{k+1}\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"39\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/4/e3480f1aa48a86bd4d5d4f1610fa2c5dea01b04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=0,1,2,\\ldots,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"128\" height=\"16\" />, determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/5/1d5acd5b4248d21e2216f12640fc8e538efdc600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/f/51fc35e4f3e07665add18dee9f1ab00f564591ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x) = (x+1)P(x) - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"190\" height=\"18\" />, and clearly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dfe7c7a0b887097fa2227a230fc915ba2e5477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> has a degree of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>Then, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/4/e3480f1aa48a86bd4d5d4f1610fa2c5dea01b04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=0,1,2,\\ldots,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"128\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/8/d389e3393a4f2bc7512e001eb6e990e62aa48941.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(k) = (k+1)P(k) - k = (k+1)\\cdot \\dfrac{k}{k+1} - k = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"395\" height=\"41\" />. \n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/4/e3480f1aa48a86bd4d5d4f1610fa2c5dea01b04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=0,1,2,\\ldots,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"128\" height=\"16\" /> are the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dfe7c7a0b887097fa2227a230fc915ba2e5477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Since these are all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> of the roots of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/c/bccff3849d9118ed8e7138a3ba529f1f7ec19c6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1^{\\text{th}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> degree polynomial, by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factor_Theorem\" title=\"Factor Theorem\">Factor Theorem</a>, we can write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dfe7c7a0b887097fa2227a230fc915ba2e5477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/7/2c7f5c20e8d498786554d56a5fc03e3046a7a14e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Q(x) = c(x)(x-1)(x-2) \\cdots (x-n)\\]\" width=\"290\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is a constant. \n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/4/d2401979e77101de3bce33c604576babf9543ea9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x+1)P(x) - x = c(x)(x-1)(x-2) \\cdots (x-n).\\]\" width=\"382\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/4/8d4c38a419ae56f13a202216dd45a1978bc91a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" /> to cancel the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/995ef484fda1fdec7303797d09386bbf45b81350.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+1)P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"20\" /> and find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00fa212950968a1b06d053c5a78f76b882a94d2b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} -(-1) &amp;= c(-1)(-1-1)(-1-2) \\cdots (-1-n) \\\\ 1 &amp;= c(-1)^{n+1}(1)(2) \\cdots (n+1) \\\\ c &amp;= (-1)^{n+1}\\dfrac{1}{(n+1)!} \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"353\" height=\"95\" />\n</p><p>Finally, plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/3/6d3e7b78ddfeecb62081cd092d3a7e60658e83b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" /> to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/5/1d5acd5b4248d21e2216f12640fc8e538efdc600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> gives: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/9/7d96af1ad2a27201cd5f4fe9651e5c01ddfe56b8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} Q(n+1)&amp;=(n+2)P(n+1)-(n+1)\\\\ (-1)^{n+1}\\dfrac{1}{(n+1)!}\\cdot(n+1)! &amp;=(n+2)P(n+1)-(n+1)\\\\ (-1)^{n+1}&amp;=(n+2)P(n+1)-(n+1)\\\\ (-1)^{n+1}+(n+1)&amp;=(n+2)P(n+1)\\\\ P(n+1) &amp;= \\dfrac{(-1)^{n+1} + (n+1)}{n+2}\\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"429\" height=\"169\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is even, this simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/3/e43ee5a9f37612182dc2f919132ad897051a2d40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n+1) = \\dfrac{n}{n+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"139\" height=\"34\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd, this simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/0/2006557e5f0e2fb9353e9d0857b3c21847150498.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n+1) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c12dda010ebddef028cda1ec9d14986f4a26d07e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Box$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"11\" />\n</p><p>~Edits by BakedPotato66\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It is fairly natural to use Lagrange's Interpolation Formula on this problem:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/a/9aa60179d1547a448341e81373ef00a0a3e2726f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} P(n+1) &amp;= \\sum_{k=0}^n \\frac{k}{k+1} \\prod_{j \\ne k} \\frac{n+1-j}{k-j} \\\\ &amp;= \\sum_{k=0}^n \\frac{k}{k+1} \\cdot \\frac{\\frac{(n+1)!}{n+1-k}}{k(k-1)(k-2) \\dots 1\\cdot (-1)(-2) \\dots (k-n)} \\\\ &amp;= \\sum_{k=0}^n \\frac{k}{k+1} (-1)^{n-k}\\cdot \\frac{(n+1)!}{k!(n+1-k)!} \\\\ &amp;= \\sum_{k=0}^n (-1)^{n-k} \\binom{n+1}{k} - \\sum_{k=0}^n \\frac{(n+1)!(-1)^{n-k}}{(k+1)!(n+1-k)!} \\\\ &amp;= -\\left(\\sum_{k=0}^{n+1} (-1)^{n+1-k} \\binom{n+1}{k} - 1\\right) + \\frac{1}{n+2} \\cdot \\sum_{k=0}^n (-1)^{n+1-k} \\binom{n+2}{k+1} \\\\ &amp;= 1 + \\frac{1}{n+2} \\left(\\sum_{k=-1}^{n+1} (-1)^{n+2 - (k+1)} \\binom{n+2}{k+1} - (-1)^{n+2} - 1\\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\boxed{1 - \\frac{(-1)^n + 1}{n+2}} \\end{align*}\" width=\"602\" height=\"412\" />\nthrough usage of the Binomial Theorem. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~lpieleanu (minor editing and reformatting)\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO\" title=\"1975 USAMO\">1975 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1975\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1975 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017143327\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.058 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 213/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1617/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6764/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   21.473      1 -total\n 49.58%   10.647      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 25.75%    5.529      1 Template:Alternat